# Project architecture

## Principles

- Simplicity before abstraction; low coupling, high cohesion; separation of concerns.
- Composition over inheritance; reuse only when there is real duplication.
- Keep domain logic out of presentational components when it grows beyond trivial UI.
- Dependencies point toward stable abstractions (types, contracts), not concrete UI.

## React / Next.js

**Prefer:** Server Components by default; Client Components only for interactivity, browser APIs, or client-only libraries. Explicit server/client boundaries. Co-located feature code. Data fetching aligned with Next.js (RSC, `fetch`, route handlers when needed).

**Avoid:** Unnecessary `"use client"`; monolithic components; business rules in JSX; deep prop drilling; premature layers (repositories, providers) before a second consumer exists.

## Structure (grow as needed)

Allow separating without mandating a heavy tree:

- `app/` — routes, layouts, server entry
- `components/` — shared UI
- `features/` — feature-specific UI + hooks
- `domain/` — types, validation schemas, pure rules
- `services/` — orchestration
- `repositories/` — data access contracts + mock/API impl
- `lib/` — utilities, shared clients

Start flat inside `app/` and `components/` until a feature justifies `features/` or `repositories/`.
